  "id": "ENT085",
  "title": "The Reference Pile Avalanche",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "creative-work struggles",
  "premise": "A maker wants to build one original toy creature, but reference cards pile so high that the workbench disappears. They select three abstract requirements from the pile, such as rolls, folds, and glows, put the cards aside, and build an original folding wheel-creature from those constraints.",
  "hook": "I can see every reference except my own idea.",
  "visible_action": "Cards stack into a wall; three verbs remain on tabs; maker clears a small workspace; a new wheel-creature unfolds and lights up.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Translate references into requirements rather than copying their surfaces.",
  "gate": "All shown reference cards must be original generic sketches; no reproduction or style imitation of established characters.",
